{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A REAPER script for browsing and editing EDL (Edit Decision List) data with a spreadsheet-style table UI, based on the Item List Browser framework.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Reads CMX3600 EDL files, displays events in an editable table, and can generate empty items with metadata on REAPER tracks for conform workflows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Workflow:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Load EDL file -> events display in table\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Browse, filter, sort, and edit metadata fields\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Load audio folder -> match files to EDL events by metadata\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Generate empty items on REAPER tracks at absolute TC positions\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Use a separate reconform script to relink original audio files\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Features:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab CMX3600 EDL parser (TITLE, FCM, events, comments)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab 15-column table: Event#, Reel, Track, Edit Type, Dissolve Len, Source TC In/Out, Record TC In/Out, Duration, Clip Name, Source File, Notes, Match Status, Matched File\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab All fields editable (except Event#, Duration, Match columns)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Excel-like selection (click, Shift+rectangle, Cmd/Ctrl multi-select)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Copy/Paste with TSV clipboard support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Multi-level sorting (click headers, Shift+click for secondary)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Text search filter (case-insensitive across all fields)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Audio file matching with BWF/iXML metadata support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Split-view UI for EDL events and audio files\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Generate empty items on REAPER tracks with P_EXT metadata\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Configurable track name format with token expansion\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Absolute timecode positioning on REAPER timeline\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Export edited EDL back to CMX3600 format\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Font size adjustment (50% - 300%)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Column presets (save/load visible column configurations)\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Supported formats:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab CMX3600 EDL (.edl) \u8212- no embedded software/version info in this format\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab XML (.xml) \u8212- FCP7-schema XMEML, read via OpenTimelineIO. Confirmed via real project files (Tools/format_tests/, 260923): - Adobe Premiere Pro export \u8212- 10/10 real samples tested were this. Detected via authoringApp="PremierePro" (NOT the /  tags near the top of the file \u8212- Premiere always writes "Final Cut Pro"/"7.0" there for schema-compat, regardless of the real authoring app; that pair is not a usable signal). - Final Cut Pro 7 / DaVinci Resolve XMEML export \u8212- same parser path, not yet exercised against a real sample from either app. UI/track-naming $\{format\} token shows all of the above simply as "XML" (see _friendly_format()); the distinction (CLB.loaded_format: "PREMIERE_XML"/"FCP7_XML"/"RESOLVE_XML") is tracked internally only.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab AAF (.aaf) \u8212- via LibAAF (aaftool) + OpenTimelineIO. Confirmed via real project files: Adobe Premiere Pro, versions 15.0.0 / 25.6.4 / 26.3.0 (read from the AAF's own Identification chain via aaf2/pyaaf2 \u8212- see Tools/format_tests/aaf_identify.py).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Subtitles / dialogue lists \u8212- no embedded software/version info: .srt SubRip absolute time .csv / .tsv Tabular dialogue lists with auto IN/OUT detection .xlsx / .xlsm Excel dialogue lists; multi-sheet picker\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Regression coverage: Tools/format_tests/ holds a golden-snapshot test harness (39 real production samples across all formats above, referenced by external path \u8212- not copied into the repo) that verifies a change to one format's parsing doesn't silently break another. Run with: lua5.4 Tools/format_tests/run_regression.lua\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires: ReaImGui (install via ReaPack) Optional: js_ReaScriptAPI (for folder selection) Required: Python 3 + opentimelineio (pip3 install opentimelineio) Optional: openpyxl (pip3 install openpyxl) \u8212- only for .xlsx subtitle import Required for AAF: aaftool in PATH (https://github.com/agfline/LibAAF)\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Converts empty items (items whose active take has no source) into real audio items by attaching a generated silent WAV. Preserves take name and item notes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Use case: Scene Cut / Picture Cut / Subtitle tracks built with empty items can now be transferred to other DAWs together with the rest of the REAPER session, because empty items are not portable but audio items are. Mimics the EdiLoad picture-cut export style (one shared file per group).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Scope: only operates on selected items. \u8226 ? Skips items that already have an audio source. \u8226 ? Active take only (multi-take items use the active take). \u8226 ? Items are grouped by track. Each group gets ONE shared silent WAV whose length equals the longest item in that group; all items in the group link to the same file. Per-item take name and notes are preserved. \u8226 ? Item D_LENGTH and D_POSITION are preserved (not overwritten by source).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Output: \u8226 ? Folder: <project_path>/Media/ \u8226 ? Format: 16-bit PCM, mono, project sample rate.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Filename rules: \u8226 ? Single item, take name has no non-ASCII chars \u8594 ? use sanitized take name. \u8226 ? Otherwise (or take name is Chinese/empty) \u8594 ? "\{TrackName\}{\i \{YYMMDDHHMM\}.wav". \u8226 ? Track name also non-ASCII/empty \u8594 ? "Track\{idx\}}\{YYMMDDHHMM\}.wav". \u8226 ? Filename collisions auto-append _2, _3, ... to avoid overwriting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Script generated and refined with Claude.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
