{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Single-button toggle watcher that add-selects media items on each track according to that track's TRACK-LEVEL Razor Areas (GUID == ""). Envelope-lane razors are preserved but ignored for matching.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MODE (user option inside the script): \u8226 ? RANGE_MODE = 1 \u8594 ? Overlap : item is selected if it INTERSECTS any Razor range \u8226 ? RANGE_MODE = 2 \u8594 ? Contain : item is selected only if it is FULLY inside a Razor range (INCLUSIVE with tiny EPS tolerance, so equal-length is selected; Pro Tools-like)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Behavior: \u8226 ? Add-only selection (does not clear existing item selection unless STRICT_SYNC = true). \u8226 ? Does not modify Razor Areas; only reads them. \u8226 ? Relaunching terminates the previous instance and keeps a toolbar toggle in sync.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note: This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Toggle (background watcher). After a right-button DRAG, on the frame the button is released (optionally one frame later) the time selection is set to the earliest start / latest end of the currently selected items. Optimized for large projects: a single pass over the selected items on release (no GUID table, no before/after diff), and an optional skip when the time selection would not change. Requires hsuanice_Mouse.lua (hsuanice Library) and the js_ReaScriptAPI extension.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-style "Link Track and Edit Selection". Edit Selection = Razor Area or Item Selection.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Perf principles: \u8226 ? Gate heavy scans by GetProjectStateChangeCount(). \u8226 ? Enumerate ONLY selected tracks/items when possible. \u8226 ? Cache per-track Razor; recompute on project-state changes only. \u8226 ? Apply changes only on delta tracks; publish ExtState only on change. \u8226 ? Keep Latched Virtual Range; avoid shrinking on track toggles.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Priority:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1)\tx360\tab Razor exists \u8594 ? use Razor (highest)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2)\tx360\tab Else Item Selection \u8594 ? use VIRTUAL (latched) span [min..max]\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3)\tx360\tab Else no active range\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes: \u8226 ? ABCD switches added (USER OPTIONS) to enable/disable each main section: A) Razor changed \u8594 ? Track selection follows "tracks with Razor" B) Items changed (no Razor) \u8594 ? Track selection follows items' tracks C) Track selection changed + REAL TS \u8594 ? build/clear Razor + sync items (Overlap) D) Razor/Track changed \u8594 ? sync items under ACTIVE range on changed tracks \u8226 ? DEBUG_PRINT will log which section fired (A/B/C/D) for instant diagnosis.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Credits: This script was generated using ChatGPT based on design concepts and iterative testing by hsuanice. hsuanice served as the workflow designer, tester, and integrator for this tool.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 After an AAF import, split-stereo tracks (e.g. "Audio 9_L" / "Audio 9_R") arrive panned center. This script scans ALL tracks and pans each adjacent L/R pair: \u8226 ? L track -> 100% Left, R track -> 100% Right \u8226 ? A pair = track N ends with an L suffix AND track N+1 has the same base name with an R suffix \u8226 ? Recognized suffixes (case-insensitive): _L/_R, -L/-R, .L/.R, " L"/" R" Unpaired L/R-looking tracks are left untouched and listed in a message for review. Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Works with every pan mode; in Dual Pan mode both knobs are set to the same side.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Single undo point.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Delete selected tracks with safety: \u8226 ? If ALL selected tracks are empty (no items, no automation/envelope data, no FX inserts, no input FX, no sends/receives) AND none is a folder parent with children, delete immediately with no prompt. \u8226 ? Otherwise (any content, folder parents with children, or FX/routing present), show a detailed summary and ask for confirmation. \u8226 ? Summary includes: selected track count, items, automation tracks, folder parents, total child tracks, FX inserts, input FX, sends, receives. Notes:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "Automation present" = any track envelope has \u8805 ?1 point OR \u8805 ?1 automation item.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab "Folder parent with children" = a selected track whose next track depth is greater than its own.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Child tracks counting includes all descendants under each selected folder parent (until depth returns to or above the parent's depth).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Master track is ignored by REAPER's CountSelectedTracks().\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
