{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Scan all non-hidden tracks and detect mixed item channel counts (1/2/3+). If confirmed, split items into separate tracks per channel group: "OriginalName Mono", "OriginalName Stereo", "OriginalName N-Ch" (N>=3). The original track is duplicated to preserve FX/routing; the duplicates are cleared via API and the relevant items are moved to them. No Fixed Lanes used. Effective channel count is taken from the source; takes with I_CHANMODE set to downmix/left/right are treated as Mono.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Real-time 24H system clock. Right-click to change color/font. Window is resizable; clock auto-scales to fill it. Settings and window geometry are remembered across sessions.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Pro Tools-style selection monitor HUD using native gfx (no ReaImGui). Top row : Items count (left) + Tracks count (right) Mid rows : Start / End / Length timecodes (PT transport style) Detail rows: MIDI / Audio / Empty + Channel Count (toggle with arrow / left-click) Right-click: font size (UI scale) / dock / close. Window position, dock state, font size, and panel state persist across restarts.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Read-only analysis script. Auto-detects project type:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Dialog Project Mode (Scene Cut track present): Combines scene data, EDL source lengths, and work log. Outputs per-scene efficiency metrics and project-wide summary. Tracks required: "Scene Cut", "EDL" (folder).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Work Log Mode (no Scene Cut track): Parses item names ("Proj | Scene | Module") to compute durations grouped by scene and module. No EDL data required.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Duration source: D_LENGTH (always). Does not write any data to the project.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Scene-aware toggle timer for the hsuanice PM system. Uses gfx (no ReaImGui). 1-second display refresh via defer + time_precise.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 State machine: IDLE \u8596 ? WORKING (no BREAK state)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Track structure (auto-managed): Scene Cut \u8592 ? folder track (I_FOLDERDEPTH = 1) 2026-03-01 \u8592 ? date track, direct child, depth = 0 2026-03-02 \u8592 ? depth = 0 DurationOnly_Log\u8592 ? last child, depth = -1; holds duration-only records\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Two work modes (auto-detected from selection): Scene Mode : a scene item on "Scene Cut" is selected P_EXT:SCENE_GUID written; name = "scene (tc) | work_type" Project Mode : no scene item selected P_EXT:SCENE_GUID not written; name = work_type only\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Work item metadata: P_EXT:SCENE_GUID (Scene Mode only), P_EXT:WORK_TYPE, P_EXT:END_REASON Duration-only items also carry P_EXT:IS_DURATION_ONLY = "1" All work items are locked (C_LOCK=1) after creation.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Monitors REAPER's "ReaScript console output" window and appends new lines to work.log.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab No changes required in other scripts.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab One log file per project folder: <project_folder>/work.log.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab If project is unsaved, uses: /../Tools/work.log.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Each appended line is prefixed with local timestamp: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requirements: - js_ReaScriptAPI extension (for reading console window text)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Notes: - This captures whatever is visible in the ReaScript console window text. - If the console is manually cleared, this daemon marks a reset in the log.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
